Package: snazzieR
Type: Package
Title: Chic and Sleek Functions for Beautiful Statisticians
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R:
    person(given = c("Aidan", "J."),
           family = "Wagner",
           email = "JesusButForGayPeople@proton.me",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Because your linear models deserve better than console output.
    A sleek color palette and kable styling to make your regression results
    look sharper than they are. Includes support for Partial Least Squares
    (PLS) regression via both the SVD and NIPALS algorithms, along with a
    unified interface for model fitting and fabulous LaTeX and console output
    formatting. Regression diagnostics include the standard residual plots,
    marginal model plots, a table of unusual observations and variance
    inflation factors. LaTeX tables also preview as HTML when R Markdown
    chunks are run interactively. See the package website at
    <https://finitesample.space/snazzier>.
